    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "questioning_technique",
      "evidence": "The interviewer repeatedly asked the patient to choose from the scale after the patient stated 'I really don't know how to answer that one,' which bordered on looping rather than acknowledging the patient's difficulty."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "flow",
      "evidence": "The transition into the PHQ-9 and GAD-7 questionnaires felt rigid, with the interviewer repeatedly restating the full question and scale options when the patient struggled, rather than simplifying the delivery."
